{% band words=["Watch.","Notice.","Capture.","Remember."] accentIndex=2 note="The verbs already lived in the launch animation; the icon only had to remember them." /%}

The identity did not need to be invented. It needed to be noticed, then held still.

{% spec columns=1 heading="The launch screen already contained the mark." standfirst="I did not want a separate logo language laid over the product. I reduced the launch motion to the four ideas that made it recognisably Aftershot." items=[{"num":"01","key":"Preserve","heading":"Preserve the Ribbon","body":"The launch screen already contained the most ownable visual idea."},{"num":"02","key":"Hold","heading":"Hold the playhead","body":"The vertical amber gesture becomes the first-read feature."},{"num":"03","key":"Leave","heading":"Leave an afterimage","body":"Unequal echo axes suggest time and persistence without becoming literal playback controls."},{"num":"04","key":"Give","heading":"Give black material","body":"Grain and a warm tonal lift keep the dark field from feeling empty."}] /%}

Every specimen below uses the same 1024-pixel production master — no separate small-size redraw. Browser presentation supplies the iOS-style corner rounding. As the icon recedes, the amber playhead reads first, the Ribbon reads second, and the grain becomes atmosphere.

