{% spec columns=1 heading="Four parts. One remembered moment." standfirst="The production icon, read as four related gestures." items=[{"num":"01","heading":"Playhead","body":"The dominant amber vertical carries immediacy and motion."},{"num":"02","heading":"Ribbon","body":"The primary horizontal axis is borrowed from the launch experience."},{"num":"03","heading":"Capture ticks","body":"The mark carries six capture ticks, with two amber annotated ticks."},{"num":"04","heading":"Echo axes","body":"Two unequal, quieter traces communicate temporal persistence rather than a menu or equaliser."}] /%}

{% spec columns=1 heading="More atmosphere. Less noise." standfirst="The first pass felt too sparse and too black. A heavier grain pass added presence, but its connected, contour-like marks fought the symbol." detail="The finer, quieter grain that survived preserves more of the launch-screen atmosphere while still reading cleanly at iPhone size." items=[{"num":"01","heading":"Find the residue","body":"The launch Ribbon supplies the underlying gesture."},{"num":"02","heading":"Test the silence","body":"The first direction feels too sparse and too black."},{"num":"03","heading":"Add material","body":"Grain gives the field presence, but connected marks compete."},{"num":"04","heading":"Quiet the noise","body":"Fine stochastic grain replaces contours; echo axes recede."},{"num":"05","heading":"Keep the atmosphere","body":"The stronger-grain finish holds up at iPhone size."}] /%}

{% swatches heading="Colour with a single job." items=[{"hex":"#000000","job":"Edge field and separation."},{"hex":"#E08A5B","job":"Playhead, annotated moments, and restrained bloom."},{"hex":"#F2F1EE","job":"Secondary geometry, used below full opacity."}] /%}

A warm-charcoal centre lift and vignette shape the black field, while photographic grain gives it material depth. Amber remains the only chromatic colour, so its single job — marking the active, captured moment — stays unmistakable.

- Warm-charcoal lift
- Fine monochrome grain
- Quiet vignette
- Restrained amber bloom

{% spec columns=1 heading="Hold the hierarchy. Preserve the quiet." items=[{"key":"Master","body":"1024×1024, opaque RGB PNG, embedded sRGB profile, exact-black perimeter, and no baked corner radius."},{"key":"Hierarchy","body":"Playhead, primary Ribbon, capture ticks, echo axes."},{"key":"Safe area","body":"Keep all essential geometry inside the central 80 percent."},{"key":"Small sizes","body":"The silhouette carries recognition; grain becomes atmosphere."},{"key":"Keep","body":"One amber accent, generous black space, varied ticks, unequal echoes, restrained bloom, and restrained vignette."},{"key":"Avoid","body":"Text, monograms, cameras, lenses, shutters, play or record buttons, literal filmstrip, extra colours, glass, gloss, neon, and transparency."}] /%}

## The moment, held.

The icon was never going to be invented from nothing. Aftershot's launch screen already had a playhead, a ribbon, and the idea of an afterimage — the work was to hold that motion still enough to sit on a Home Screen and mean the same thing at rest that it means mid-capture.
